\section{Interpretation and sampling bias}{

Background (pseudo-absence) points define an arbitrary reference prevalence,
so downstream model outputs are \strong{relative habitat suitability}, not
calibrated probabilities of occurrence: changing \code{ratio} shifts predicted
values up or down without changing their spatial ranking. Presence records
are also subject to sampling bias (accessibility, survey effort); unless
corrected, the models partly describe where the species was \emph{observed}
rather than where it \emph{occurs}. Carry both caveats into any HSS, effect, or
projection interpretation.
}

